    </p>

    <h2>Where You Stay in Lisbon Matters</h2>

    <p>
      How many days you have is only part of the planning decision.
    </p>

    <p>
      Where you stay can change how those days feel.
    </p>

    <p>
      A centrally located hotel can make it easier to move between neighborhoods
      and return during the day. A hotel in one of Lisbon’s older neighborhoods may
      offer more atmosphere but also involve hills, stairs or more complicated
      luggage logistics.
    </p>

    <p>
      There is no single Lisbon neighborhood that is right for everyone.
    </p>

    <p>The more useful question is:</p>

    <blockquote>
      <p>
        <strong>
          What kind of Lisbon experience do you want your hotel location to support?
        </strong>
      </p>
    </blockquote>

    <aside class="hotel-recommendation">
